<title>SPAIN: Spain praises labour reform proposals.</title>
<headline>Spain praises labour reform proposals.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Labour Minister Javier Arenas on Wednesday praised labour reform proposals agreed between unions and employers which he said would bring more stability to the labour market.</p>
<p>&quot;I am sure this reform will end the abuse of temporary contracts and promote more stable employment,&quot; he told a news conference.</p>
<p>Unions and employers presented their labour reform proposals on Wednesday after months of intense talks.</p>
<p>Arenas said the government would adopt the reforms as soon as possible.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2161</p>
